    "raw": "Phase changes: 594.26 K, melting point of Cd; $\\Delta H^{\\circ} = 1.480$ kcal/mol. \n1040 K, boiling point of Cd; $\\Delta H^{\\circ} = 23.809$ kcal/mol. \nHeat capacity (cal/mol·K) and enthalpy (kcal/mol) equations: \n<table><tr><td rowspan=\"2\">298.15-1100 K:</td><td> $Cp^o$  = 11.693 + 1.476x $10^{-3}$ T - 0.738x $10^5$ T $^{-2}$ </td></tr><tr><td> $H^o-H_{298}^o$  = 11.693x $10^{-3}$ T + 0.738x $10^{-6}$ T $^2$  + 0.738x $10^2$ T $^{-1}$  - 3.799</td></tr></table>\nReaction equations (kcal/mol): \n<table><tr><td rowspan=\"2\">298.15-594.26 K:</td><td> $\\Delta Hr^{\\circ} = -51.773 + 2.202 \\times 10^{-3} \\text{T} - 0.868 \\times 10^{-6} \\text{T}^{2} + 41.250 \\text{T}^{-1}$ </td></tr><tr><td> $\\Delta Gr^{\\circ} = -51.773 - 2.202 \\times 10^{-3} \\text{T} \\ln T + 0.868 \\times 10^{-6} \\text{T}^{2} + 20.625 \\text{T}^{-1} + 36.847 \\times 10^{-3} \\text{T}$ </td></tr><tr><td rowspan=\"2\">594.26-1040 K:</td><td> $\\Delta Hr^{\\circ} = -52.699 + 0.416 \\times 10^{-3} \\text{T} + 0.578 \\times 10^{-6} \\text{T}^{2} + 39.650 \\text{T}^{-1}$ </td></tr><tr><td> $\\Delta Gr^{\\circ} = -52.699 - 0.416 \\times 10^{-3} \\text{T} \\ln T - 0.578 \\times 10^{-6} \\text{T}^{2} + 19.825 \\text{T}^{-1} + 27.860 \\times 10^{-3} \\text{T}$ </td></tr><tr><td rowspan=\"2\">1040-1100 K:</td><td> $\\Delta Hr^{\\circ} = -78.731 + 2.553 \\times 10^{-3} \\text{T} + 0.578 \\times 10^{-6} \\text{T}^{2} + 39.650 \\text{T}^{-1}$ </td></tr><tr><td> $\\Delta Gr^{\\circ} = -78.731 - 2.553 \\times 10^{-3} \\text{T} \\ln T - 0.578 \\times 10^{-6} \\text{T}^{2} + 19.825 \\text{T}^{-1} + 67.736 \\times 10^{-3} \\text{T}$ </td></tr></table>\nSources: Enthalpy of formation at 298 K from Adami (1). All other data from Beyer (9). ",
